---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="synterr-nlp"
  description="Open Russian grammatical error correction. Rule-grounded synthetic data, per-rule diagnostics, reproducible pipelines."
  wide={true}
>
  <!-- Hero ------------------------------------------------------------ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1>Russian grammatical error correction, evaluated honestly.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Most GEC benchmarks summarize heterogeneous behavior into one F-score
        and miss the parts where models silently regress. We build the
        rule-grounded synthetic data and per-rule diagnostics that surface
        what aggregate metrics hide.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/papers/bea-2026/overview/">Read the BEA 2026 overview</a>
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="https://github.com/synterr-nlp/synterr" rel="external">Code on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-fig">
      <img src="/papers/bea-2026/figures/depparse_errors.svg"
           alt="A Russian sentence with three rule-grounded error sites annotated on its dependency tree." />
      <figcaption>
        Three rule-grounded error sites on one sentence: agreement
        (<code>amod</code>), subordinate-clause boundary (<code>acl:relcl</code>),
        case government (<code>obl</code>).
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- Featured paper -------------------------------------------------- -->
  <section class="featured">
    <div class="kicker">Featured · accepted at ACL BEA 2026</div>
    <h2 class="featured-title">What Aggregate Scores Hide</h2>
    <p class="featured-blurb">
      Across eight open models from 0.8B to 12B parameters, fine-tuning on
      synthetic data raises overall F<sub>0.5</sub> on LoRuGEC, but drives
      subordinate-clause comma accuracy from 14% to 1%. Aggregate scores
      can't detect this; per-rule diagnostics can. Once detected, it's
      fixable.
    </p>
    <ul class="featured-links">
      <li><a href="/papers/bea-2026/overview/">Graphical overview</a></li>
      <li><a href="/papers/bea-2026/">Paper landing</a></li>
      <li><a href="/papers/bea-2026/tables/per-rule/">Per-rule data</a></li>
      <li><a href="/papers/bea-2026/tables/reasoning-9b/">Reasoning chains</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- What we do ------------------------------------------------------ -->
  <section class="threecol">
    <article>
      <h3>Synterr</h3>
      <p>
        An open-source synthetic-error generator for Russian.
        Configurable per-rule rates, dependency-tree-grounded handlers,
        a 98-category taxonomy from Rozental's reference grammar.
      </p>
      <p class="link">
        <a href="/synterr/">Read the docs</a>
        &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="https://github.com/synterr-nlp/synterr" rel="external">GitHub</a>
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Per-rule diagnostics</h3>
      <p>
        Browsable taxonomy and per-rule scores for evaluating Russian GEC
        systems honestly. Cell-coloured xlsx parsed natively in your
        browser. Sortable, filterable, downloadable.
      </p>
      <p class="link">
        <a href="/papers/bea-2026/tables/cross-reference/">Browse the taxonomy</a>
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Reproducible pipelines</h3>
      <p>
        Every released dataset comes with pinned generation commit, SHA-256
        checksums, and a verifier script. v4 SFT data is byte-verified
        against the file the paper trained on.
      </p>
      <p class="link">
        <a href="https://github.com/synterr-nlp/synterr/blob/master/data/V4_DATA_PROVENANCE.md" rel="external">v4 provenance</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <!-- Latest activity ------------------------------------------------- -->
  <section class="activity">
    <h2>Recent</h2>
    <ul class="timeline">
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-05-09">2026-05-09</time>
        <span><strong>Site online.</strong> Browsable tables, reasoning-chain viewer, graphical overview.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-05-01">2026-05-01</time>
        <span><strong>Synterr v1.0.</strong> Paper-release tag with reproducibility pack (checksums, verify script, pinned commit).</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-05-04">2026-05-04</time>
        <span><strong>BEA 2026 acceptance.</strong> "What Aggregate Scores Hide" accepted at the 21st BEA workshop.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-03-22">2026-03-22</time>
        <span><strong>v4 dataset frozen.</strong> 39,209 SFT examples, deterministic build pipeline.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 4rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .hero .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
  }
  .hero-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .btn-primary, .btn-secondary {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: none;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: white;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: white;
  }
  .btn-secondary {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .btn-secondary:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .hero-fig {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .hero-fig img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: white;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .hero-fig figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .hero-fig code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 0 0.25rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  /* ── Featured ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .featured {
    margin: 4rem 0;
    padding: 2rem 2.25rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border-radius: 6px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .featured-title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .featured-blurb {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .featured-links {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .featured-links li::before {
    content: "→";
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-right: 0.4rem;
  }

  /* ── Three column "what we do" ────────────────────────── */
  .threecol {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    margin: 4rem 0;
  }
  .threecol h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .threecol p {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .threecol p.link {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* ── Activity timeline ────────────────────────────────── */
  .activity {
    margin: 4rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .activity h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .timeline li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .timeline li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .timeline time {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .timeline span { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .timeline strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; }
    .threecol { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .timeline li { grid-template-columns: 5rem 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; }
  }
</style>
